1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,720
Once someone opens the door, follow whatever directions they give you.

2
00:00:09,560 --> 00:00:12,040
It was a lot of fun. Now good luck to you.

3
00:00:12,720 --> 00:00:13,700
Yeah, thanks.

4
00:00:18,680 --> 00:00:21,040
Hey, does someone named Mihail live here?

5
00:00:22,060 --> 00:00:24,860
Go do some shopping at Deke Sakura by the station.

6
00:00:25,740 --> 00:00:27,340
Use this card at the checkout.

7
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,540
Very good, sir. Please follow me this way.

8
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:02,000
Thank you.

9
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,000
Thank you.

10
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:05,000
There's a lot more people than last year.

11
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:25,220
There's a lot more people than last year.

12
00:02:25,220 --> 00:02:31,720
Wonder if there's anybody I know.

13
00:02:34,220 --> 00:02:34,820
Hey!

14
00:02:35,220 --> 00:02:37,320
You walked all over us last year.

15
00:02:37,620 --> 00:02:39,800
But it's gonna be a lot different this time.

16
00:02:40,020 --> 00:02:43,280
We all put ourselves through some intense training after what happened.

17
00:02:43,760 --> 00:02:46,720
Now our team works perfect, so good luck trying to...

18
00:02:46,720 --> 00:02:51,720
Thanks for coming, everyone.

19
00:02:53,220 --> 00:02:57,740
This year, 1,489 applicants have made it this far.

20
00:02:57,960 --> 00:03:02,380
But the examiner for the second phase asked me to trim that number down to about 300.

21
00:03:03,280 --> 00:03:07,200
But as for the exam itself, lunch is two hours away.

22
00:03:07,460 --> 00:03:09,840
So knock out five people before then.

23
00:03:09,840 --> 00:03:13,900
Once all five are down, grab their badges and come see me.

24
00:03:14,420 --> 00:03:16,500
I'll be right on the other side of the door.

25
00:03:16,900 --> 00:03:17,480
All right.

26
00:03:17,820 --> 00:03:20,560
As soon as it closes, that's your cue to get started.

27
00:03:25,980 --> 00:03:28,760
Every face of the exam should be like this.

28
00:03:29,880 --> 00:03:33,620
A hunter's gotta be strong, and this helps find and weed out the weaklings.

29
00:03:33,620 --> 00:03:42,420
You're here too, old man.

30
00:03:42,760 --> 00:03:46,720
Sucks for you.

31
00:03:47,240 --> 00:03:48,280
I'll pass this year.

32
00:03:48,640 --> 00:03:49,460
And just me.

33
00:03:50,620 --> 00:03:53,000
He's totally out of our league.

34
00:03:54,060 --> 00:03:56,760
That kid was born to be a top-rate hunter.

35
00:03:57,760 --> 00:04:01,640
This will be our last year trying out for the hunter exam.

36
00:04:03,620 --> 00:04:12,020
Took you long enough.

37
00:04:12,580 --> 00:04:15,240
It's already been a full hour and a half.

38
00:04:15,520 --> 00:04:16,680
What are the others doing?

39
00:04:17,240 --> 00:04:18,480
They're all asleep.

40
00:04:19,760 --> 00:04:20,360
Huh?

41
00:04:21,160 --> 00:04:23,620
It just took me a little while to collect all the badges.

42
00:04:26,260 --> 00:04:29,180
What now?

43
00:04:29,480 --> 00:04:30,120
Second phase?

44
00:04:30,120 --> 00:04:35,220
That won't be necessary, I'm afraid.

45
00:04:35,400 --> 00:04:38,420
He's already demonstrated his skill quite sufficiently.

46
00:04:40,220 --> 00:04:42,580
Killua, inhabitant of the shadows.

47
00:04:43,140 --> 00:04:45,940
He's certainly matured since we saw him last.

48
00:04:46,900 --> 00:04:49,400
Applicant 1219, Killua.

49
00:04:50,260 --> 00:04:50,760
Here.

50
00:04:50,760 --> 00:04:52,200
Congratulations.

51
00:04:54,200 --> 00:04:55,420
You passed.

52
00:04:55,420 --> 00:05:03,020
Welcome back, Killua.

53
00:05:03,240 --> 00:05:03,980
How was it?

54
00:05:04,380 --> 00:05:06,180
Well, I aced it in no time, naturally.

55
00:05:07,320 --> 00:05:07,820
Yeah!

56
00:05:07,820 --> 00:05:13,080
I'm sorry to interrupt your celebration, but take a look at these spell cards.

57
00:05:15,240 --> 00:05:15,720
Wow.

58
00:05:16,100 --> 00:05:17,700
There's even an S-rank card.

59
00:05:17,980 --> 00:05:19,900
So how much do you think we can sell it for?

60
00:05:20,420 --> 00:05:22,760
I'm not sure, but why don't we go and ask around?

61
00:05:23,120 --> 00:05:23,460
No.

62
00:05:23,800 --> 00:05:24,980
We should use it wisely.

63
00:05:26,040 --> 00:05:27,420
So what do you think, Killua?

64
00:05:27,980 --> 00:05:29,580
I guess it's safe to hold onto it.

65
00:05:30,580 --> 00:05:33,240
It's not going to get stolen with all these defensive spells.

66
00:05:34,720 --> 00:05:36,580
Have you guys tried any of these out yet?

67
00:05:36,900 --> 00:05:38,280
Just the blackout curtain one.

68
00:05:38,880 --> 00:05:39,800
Why only one?

69
00:05:39,980 --> 00:05:41,840
Why even have them if you don't use them?

70
00:05:42,580 --> 00:05:42,900
Here.

71
00:05:43,500 --> 00:05:44,820
Start off by using this one.

72
00:05:45,360 --> 00:05:48,180
It lets you choose any player you've met and have a talk with them.

73
00:05:49,560 --> 00:05:50,700
Who should we talk to?

74
00:05:51,200 --> 00:05:52,900
First, let's look at who's available.

75
00:05:53,620 --> 00:05:55,020
Alright, contact on!

76
00:05:55,020 --> 00:06:02,440
I didn't know there'd be so many.

77
00:06:05,940 --> 00:06:08,220
Hey, when'd you run into him?

78
00:06:08,820 --> 00:06:09,140
Huh?

79
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:15,440
Chrollo!

80
00:06:16,260 --> 00:06:17,780
Hold on, who's Chrollo?

81
00:06:18,120 --> 00:06:19,060
I haven't seen him.

82
00:06:19,400 --> 00:06:21,000
Well, not inside of the game anyway.

83
00:06:21,580 --> 00:06:23,820
Does that mean you passed each other without noticing?

84
00:06:23,820 --> 00:06:25,580
What are you two talking about?

85
00:06:25,940 --> 00:06:27,120
But I don't get it.

86
00:06:27,360 --> 00:06:29,980
I could have sworn Kurapika sealed his nen, didn't he?

87
00:06:30,420 --> 00:06:31,260
He sure did.

88
00:06:31,540 --> 00:06:34,020
And you have to use nen just to get inside the game.

89
00:06:34,320 --> 00:06:35,540
Who is this Kurapika?

90
00:06:35,820 --> 00:06:37,620
If that's the case, then that means...

91
00:06:37,620 --> 00:06:38,280
Come on!

92
00:06:38,340 --> 00:06:40,440
What the hell are you guys talking about?

93
00:06:42,820 --> 00:06:45,360
Oh, I get it now.

94
00:06:45,480 --> 00:06:46,520
That's what's going on.

95
00:06:46,740 --> 00:06:48,980
It isn't funny.

96
00:06:49,360 --> 00:06:50,880
Just explain to us what's happening.

97
00:06:50,880 --> 00:06:52,540
Sorry about that.

98
00:06:53,960 --> 00:06:55,700
This probably isn't the boss.

99
00:06:56,520 --> 00:06:58,820
He hasn't exorcised the nen from his body.

100
00:07:00,360 --> 00:07:00,800
Exorcism?

101
00:07:00,940 --> 00:07:01,900
It's quite possible.

102
00:07:02,500 --> 00:07:03,020
It is?

103
00:07:03,180 --> 00:07:03,720
Of course.

104
00:07:04,060 --> 00:07:08,240
If you're able to place nen on others, there would have to be a way to remove it as well.

105
00:07:09,100 --> 00:07:13,100
So does that mean that Chrollo removed Kurapika's nen and then entered the game?

106
00:07:13,520 --> 00:07:14,780
Why would he come here?

107
00:07:14,780 --> 00:07:18,600
I've got no idea, but we should probably let Kurapika know.

108
00:07:19,380 --> 00:07:21,320
In that case, I'm going to hop out of the game again.

109
00:07:21,740 --> 00:07:23,540
Why don't you use a spell card to leave?

110
00:07:24,660 --> 00:07:25,600
Hold on to it.

111
00:07:25,920 --> 00:07:27,400
I'll be back in four hours.

112
00:07:29,240 --> 00:07:31,100
I should have realized it sooner.

113
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:34,720
Fact is, this island is due east of York New City.

114
00:07:35,220 --> 00:07:35,860
Straight shot.

115
00:07:35,860 --> 00:07:40,700
Perhaps to the east one can be tracked.

116
00:07:41,220 --> 00:07:43,380
The one most needed you're sure to find.

117
00:07:43,800 --> 00:07:44,360
I see.

118
00:07:44,780 --> 00:07:47,540
The boss came to find someone to exorcise that nen.

119
00:07:48,360 --> 00:07:52,520
He probably arrived here the same way we did, but then Razor kicked him out.

120
00:07:52,860 --> 00:07:55,540
I assume that's when he realized this was Greed Island.

121
00:07:56,200 --> 00:08:00,980
But now that the boss can't use nen anymore, he can't enter through the usual channels.

122
00:08:00,980 --> 00:08:05,100
So he must have hired someone to come to the island for him.

123
00:08:05,720 --> 00:08:09,800
And he had them use his name as a hidden message for the rest of us.

124
00:08:11,640 --> 00:08:14,980
The exorcist is on Greed Island.

125
00:08:17,060 --> 00:08:19,100
Another change in plans, huh?

126
00:08:19,840 --> 00:08:21,700
Let's bring everybody else out here.

127
00:08:22,020 --> 00:08:22,760
I agree.

128
00:08:23,100 --> 00:08:25,180
Then all of us will look for the exorcist.

129
00:08:25,360 --> 00:08:26,940
One small correction.

130
00:08:26,940 --> 00:08:27,460
Huh?

131
00:08:30,980 --> 00:08:31,780
It's you.

132
00:08:32,240 --> 00:08:32,720
Hisoka!

133
00:08:33,900 --> 00:08:37,360
See, using Chrollo's name was actually my idea.

134
00:08:37,900 --> 00:08:41,140
But I didn't know that entering any name you like was an option.

135
00:08:41,560 --> 00:08:44,680
Or at least not until I had already gotten inside.

136
00:08:45,560 --> 00:08:47,600
You should be praising my initiative.

137
00:08:48,180 --> 00:08:51,260
If not for me, you never would have understood Chrollo's message.

138
00:08:51,840 --> 00:08:54,120
So that's what this is all about, huh?

139
00:08:54,740 --> 00:08:57,460
I've got half a mind to kill you right here and now.

140
00:08:57,460 --> 00:08:59,480
But I'll leave that to the boss.

141
00:08:59,480 --> 00:09:04,640
Well, if I can help further use contact to find me.

142
00:09:05,060 --> 00:09:07,980
And I'll let you know if I happen to learn anything new.

143
00:09:09,380 --> 00:09:10,420
So long.

144
00:09:13,540 --> 00:09:16,020
I didn't think the boss would have hired Hisoka.

145
00:09:16,420 --> 00:09:18,880
Guess he didn't have much of a choice, but still.

146
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:22,120
I'm betting that he offered him a duel, post-exorcism.

147
00:09:22,780 --> 00:09:23,260
Probably.

148
00:09:23,260 --> 00:09:28,100
But now it's only a matter of time until the boss comes back.

149
00:09:28,100 --> 00:09:32,480
I doubt it.

150
00:09:32,480 --> 00:09:38,100
If he or one of the other spiders were to attempt to remove my Nen, I would know about it immediately.

151
00:09:38,380 --> 00:09:39,880
There's no other way around it.

152
00:09:40,480 --> 00:09:44,240
So when you set up your ability, you took something like this into account?

153
00:09:44,980 --> 00:09:46,080
Of course I did.

154
00:09:46,220 --> 00:09:48,080
If you're able to place Nen on others.

155
00:09:48,520 --> 00:09:51,940
It stands to reason that the ability to remove it exists as well.

156
00:09:52,300 --> 00:09:53,440
It's common sense.

157
00:09:53,440 --> 00:09:57,180
Well, just thought I'd let you know.

158
00:09:57,500 --> 00:09:59,200
You can do whatever you want with it.

159
00:09:59,780 --> 00:10:00,860
I appreciate that.

160
00:10:01,180 --> 00:10:02,040
You have my gratitude.

161
00:10:06,540 --> 00:10:07,760
Did you need anything?

162
00:10:07,760 --> 00:10:12,540
What am I supposed to do?

163
00:10:13,480 --> 00:10:15,220
What will I do this month?

164
00:10:16,540 --> 00:10:17,720
Please, tell me.

165
00:10:18,440 --> 00:10:19,880
What should I do now?

166
00:10:20,500 --> 00:10:21,880
It's going to be alright.

167
00:10:22,160 --> 00:10:23,240
Just let me handle it.

168
00:10:23,360 --> 00:10:24,680
What do you know about it?

169
00:10:25,100 --> 00:10:28,880
What the hell good are you if you have no idea what's going to happen in the future?

170
00:10:29,980 --> 00:10:31,900
Nihon, I need her.

171
00:10:32,520 --> 00:10:33,860
Restore her at once.

172
00:10:36,020 --> 00:10:36,780
Damn it.

173
00:10:36,780 --> 00:10:38,920
How could this have happened?

174
00:10:42,200 --> 00:10:43,820
I wonder what's wrong.

175
00:10:45,460 --> 00:10:47,720
Why did it stop coming out all of a sudden?

176
00:10:50,200 --> 00:10:50,880
See ya!

177
00:10:54,300 --> 00:10:56,920
Well, it looks like it's not the real Prolulu Silver.

178
00:10:57,500 --> 00:10:58,380
Wait, it's not?

179
00:10:58,860 --> 00:10:59,800
Talk to Kurapika.

180
00:11:00,260 --> 00:11:01,480
He was pretty calm about it.

181
00:11:01,880 --> 00:11:04,560
By the way he responded, he didn't sound concerned.

182
00:11:04,560 --> 00:11:07,680
It sounds like you got all worked up over nothing.

183
00:11:08,100 --> 00:11:11,360
Now if you ask me, you should get back to focusing on yourselves.

184
00:11:11,780 --> 00:11:12,180
Us!

185
00:11:12,380 --> 00:11:13,420
Start with the basics.

186
00:11:14,260 --> 00:11:15,720
We're not going to train.

187
00:11:16,240 --> 00:11:17,500
We've gotten distracted.

188
00:11:17,500 --> 00:11:20,680
But it's time we start trying to beat this game.

189
00:11:20,680 --> 00:11:37,260
It's said that the legendary King White Stag Beetle lives only in this tree.

190
00:11:37,960 --> 00:11:39,940
And that there's only one way to capture it.

191
00:11:40,720 --> 00:11:42,280
Hit the tree and shake it out.

192
00:11:42,280 --> 00:11:45,440
Show me rock!

193
00:11:45,820 --> 00:11:47,040
John can't rock!

194
00:11:49,500 --> 00:11:54,620
Oh wow!

195
00:11:54,840 --> 00:11:56,300
It's raining bugs everywhere!

196
00:11:57,740 --> 00:11:58,520
Found it!

197
00:11:58,900 --> 00:12:00,100
Difficulty reg A.

198
00:12:00,100 --> 00:12:01,360
Oh right!

199
00:12:01,560 --> 00:12:03,860
That makes three King White Stag Beetle cards!

200
00:12:04,520 --> 00:12:07,300
You know, you could have gotten more if you'd just thrown a real punch.

201
00:12:07,940 --> 00:12:09,300
Yeah, you're probably right.

202
00:12:09,380 --> 00:12:10,840
But I didn't want to damage the tree.

203
00:12:13,100 --> 00:12:15,220
There is no such girl here in this mansion.

204
00:12:15,900 --> 00:12:18,900
And even if there were, you would never be able to find her.

205
00:12:19,060 --> 00:12:21,880
Not with all the traps that you would have to get past first.

206
00:12:22,040 --> 00:12:22,640
Found her!

207
00:12:22,640 --> 00:12:25,940
She was hidden in a room deep underground.

208
00:12:26,520 --> 00:12:26,980
What?

209
00:12:27,260 --> 00:12:28,260
Damn you!

210
00:12:28,800 --> 00:12:31,680
A gold dust girl.

211
00:12:32,220 --> 00:12:32,980
Rank A!

212
00:12:33,200 --> 00:12:35,040
But the guard was only an F rank.

213
00:12:35,840 --> 00:12:38,600
Next, let's head to Darius, the gambling town.

214
00:12:39,340 --> 00:12:41,260
Oh man, the Antokiba contest.

215
00:12:41,680 --> 00:12:43,140
That's supposed to be today, right?

216
00:12:43,360 --> 00:12:45,560
We're passing through, so let's give it a try.

217
00:12:47,420 --> 00:12:50,380
The winner this month is Team Killua and Gon!

218
00:12:50,800 --> 00:12:52,140
A paladin's necklace!

219
00:12:52,140 --> 00:12:52,840
Score!

220
00:12:54,020 --> 00:12:56,680
Hey, I don't think I get what this description means.

221
00:12:56,940 --> 00:12:58,480
Let's go ask one of the shopkeepers.

222
00:12:59,300 --> 00:13:01,920
When you wear this necklace, then you're impervious.

223
00:13:02,440 --> 00:13:05,200
It reflects all of the attack spells directed at you.

224
00:13:05,580 --> 00:13:06,520
And that isn't all.

225
00:13:06,940 --> 00:13:10,880
If you find that any of your cards are under the effects of either the clone or fake cards,

226
00:13:11,220 --> 00:13:12,840
you can restore them with a touch.

227
00:13:13,620 --> 00:13:14,300
Hear that?

228
00:13:14,640 --> 00:13:17,680
If we wear this, we won't have to worry about losing any cards.

229
00:13:20,300 --> 00:13:21,720
Okay, memory helmet?

230
00:13:22,140 --> 00:13:29,540
Witch's love potion, risky dice, king white stag beetle, gold dust girl, and paladin's necklace.

231
00:13:29,540 --> 00:13:33,420
A total of six different specified slot cards.

232
00:13:33,920 --> 00:13:34,920
Piece of cake, huh?

233
00:13:35,580 --> 00:13:36,540
Piece of cake?

234
00:13:36,700 --> 00:13:37,620
Not at all.

235
00:13:37,960 --> 00:13:41,060
This was only possible because of your grueling training.

236
00:13:43,160 --> 00:13:43,500
Huh?

237
00:13:43,500 --> 00:13:44,960
Attention.

238
00:13:44,960 --> 00:13:47,740
Another player has cast contact on you.

239
00:13:49,040 --> 00:13:50,080
Hey, Gon!

240
00:13:50,340 --> 00:13:51,160
It's been a while.

241
00:13:51,880 --> 00:13:52,540
Who are you?

242
00:13:53,960 --> 00:13:55,420
What, you don't remember me?

243
00:13:55,860 --> 00:13:59,380
Well, what about the player who took the Sword of Truth from you in Antakiba?

244
00:13:59,760 --> 00:14:00,600
Remember him?

245
00:14:00,600 --> 00:14:02,960
What do you want?

246
00:14:03,400 --> 00:14:04,400
Up for a trade?

247
00:14:05,020 --> 00:14:08,560
I have number 66, the witch's diet pills, and 27.

248
00:14:08,880 --> 00:14:10,840
That one is the book of VIP passes.

249
00:14:11,520 --> 00:14:13,380
You can talk it over with your friends.

250
00:14:14,220 --> 00:14:15,340
What do you think?

251
00:14:15,340 --> 00:14:22,480
Attention.

252
00:14:23,040 --> 00:14:25,240
Another player has cast contact on you.

253
00:14:26,360 --> 00:14:27,300
Tescara here.

254
00:14:27,400 --> 00:14:28,700
Oh, you again, huh?

255
00:14:29,400 --> 00:14:32,580
Interested in trading your angel's breath for our patch of forest?

256
00:14:33,360 --> 00:14:34,980
It's an SS rank card.

257
00:14:35,520 --> 00:14:36,440
Yeah, no thanks.

258
00:14:36,740 --> 00:14:39,600
As I've already said, I have no desire to deal with you.

259
00:14:39,940 --> 00:14:41,420
What if I throw in a clone?

260
00:14:42,200 --> 00:14:44,500
I thought I made it clear there's no deal here.

261
00:14:45,160 --> 00:14:47,360
You already have 92 different cards.

262
00:14:47,780 --> 00:14:50,900
All that's left are the ones monopolized by the other players.

263
00:14:51,500 --> 00:14:52,540
Isn't that right?

264
00:14:54,160 --> 00:14:56,160
Actually, we have 95.

265
00:14:56,980 --> 00:14:58,820
I'm sure you have some of the items,

266
00:14:58,940 --> 00:15:01,300
and you're waiting for someone else to use gain on them.

267
00:15:01,300 --> 00:15:07,100
In fact, it's entirely possible that Angel's Breath is the last card that you need to obtain.

268
00:15:07,100 --> 00:15:13,640
And I can't think of a single reason we would give that to you and lose the game in the process.

269
00:15:14,740 --> 00:15:16,320
Stop playing, Dome.

270
00:15:17,780 --> 00:15:23,780
I happen to know that you and your people are currently monopolizing both Angel's Breath and Nightjade,

271
00:15:23,960 --> 00:15:26,020
which means the game is not over yet.

272
00:15:26,500 --> 00:15:26,800
Oh.

273
00:15:26,800 --> 00:15:29,620
I wish you boys the best of luck,

274
00:15:29,920 --> 00:15:32,540
but we're never going to let you have these cards.

275
00:15:32,660 --> 00:15:33,800
And if I offer three,

276
00:15:34,860 --> 00:15:36,040
the patch of forest,

277
00:15:36,540 --> 00:15:37,700
spirited away hollow,

278
00:15:38,080 --> 00:15:39,660
and then to top it all off,

279
00:15:39,880 --> 00:15:41,180
there's miniature dragon.

280
00:15:42,260 --> 00:15:44,600
And you only have to give us Nightjade,

281
00:15:44,780 --> 00:15:45,800
not Angel's Breath.

282
00:15:46,740 --> 00:15:50,360
We'd be giving you one SS rank and two S rank,

283
00:15:50,660 --> 00:15:52,440
while you'd only give up an A rank.

284
00:15:52,720 --> 00:15:54,420
That's too good to pass up.

285
00:15:56,720 --> 00:15:58,960
We'll need a little time to discuss it.

286
00:15:59,340 --> 00:16:01,720
To be clear, this is our final offer.

287
00:16:02,160 --> 00:16:03,820
We won't negotiate any further.

288
00:16:04,840 --> 00:16:05,260
Book.

289
00:16:06,860 --> 00:16:08,300
It's gotta be a trap.

290
00:16:08,540 --> 00:16:09,900
It's too good to be true.

291
00:16:10,520 --> 00:16:12,080
Tisgera is awfully cautious.

292
00:16:12,600 --> 00:16:14,860
I doubt he's looking to pick a fight with us.

293
00:16:15,220 --> 00:16:16,000
But that said,

294
00:16:16,060 --> 00:16:18,620
he's not the type to make a losing deal, either.

295
00:16:18,980 --> 00:16:21,200
Which must mean he thinks he can obtain

296
00:16:21,200 --> 00:16:22,900
an Angel's Breath on his own.

297
00:16:23,640 --> 00:16:24,380
What do you think?

298
00:16:24,840 --> 00:16:26,920
I mean, there are 40 types of spell cards.

299
00:16:27,120 --> 00:16:28,140
Does he have all of them?

300
00:16:28,540 --> 00:16:29,580
Maybe, if so.

301
00:16:29,880 --> 00:16:31,540
They're just waiting for us to use gain

302
00:16:31,540 --> 00:16:33,080
on one of our Angel's Breaths.

303
00:16:33,720 --> 00:16:34,380
Could be.

304
00:16:34,700 --> 00:16:36,220
But it took a whole lot of hard work

305
00:16:36,220 --> 00:16:37,640
to monopolize Nightjade.

306
00:16:38,280 --> 00:16:40,080
If one of the cards got destroyed,

307
00:16:40,360 --> 00:16:42,900
one of our Jade jewels would turn back into a card.

308
00:16:42,900 --> 00:16:46,640
Those guys might be able to get their hands

309
00:16:46,640 --> 00:16:48,520
on an SS-rank Angel's Breaths,

310
00:16:48,600 --> 00:16:50,020
but the A-ranked Nightjade

311
00:16:50,020 --> 00:16:52,180
is a lot harder for them to get.

312
00:16:53,360 --> 00:16:55,060
This is a real gamble.

313
00:17:02,740 --> 00:17:03,260
Book.

314
00:17:04,840 --> 00:17:05,540
See ya.

315
00:17:05,540 --> 00:17:15,240
That was surprisingly uneventful.

316
00:17:15,460 --> 00:17:17,020
It was kind of a letdown, actually.

317
00:17:17,660 --> 00:17:18,980
I was so nervous.

318
00:17:19,840 --> 00:17:22,260
But that's seven types in just three days.

319
00:17:22,960 --> 00:17:24,400
We're making real progress.

320
00:17:24,980 --> 00:17:26,640
Okay, let's keep it up.

321
00:17:27,360 --> 00:17:28,700
Are there any other events

322
00:17:28,700 --> 00:17:30,340
for getting restricted slot cards?

323
00:17:30,900 --> 00:17:33,160
Uh, I think there are,

324
00:17:33,160 --> 00:17:34,080
but let me see.

325
00:17:35,540 --> 00:17:36,880
Prizes from the slots?

326
00:17:37,580 --> 00:17:39,360
Well, it is the city of gambling.

327
00:17:40,180 --> 00:17:42,940
You have a 0.01% chance of winning.

328
00:17:43,300 --> 00:17:44,880
That's just one in 10,000.

329
00:17:45,080 --> 00:17:46,680
So it all comes down to luck.

330
00:17:46,900 --> 00:17:48,000
That's pretty risky.

331
00:17:48,900 --> 00:17:49,420
I know.

332
00:17:49,980 --> 00:17:51,700
Hey, Gon, use that dice.

333
00:17:52,380 --> 00:17:55,160
Now, if we get great luck, we can win.

334
00:17:55,540 --> 00:17:57,000
But if you roll worse luck,

335
00:17:57,120 --> 00:17:58,580
something so bad's gonna happen

336
00:17:58,580 --> 00:18:00,260
that it'll cancel out everything good

337
00:18:00,260 --> 00:18:01,200
that's happened to us.

338
00:18:01,200 --> 00:18:04,120
Yeah, but there's only a 1 in 20 chance of that, right?

339
00:18:06,960 --> 00:18:07,400
Yes!

340
00:18:08,320 --> 00:18:10,240
All we gotta do is spin the wheel!

341
00:18:13,240 --> 00:18:13,640
Wow!

342
00:18:14,620 --> 00:18:14,980
Awesome!

343
00:18:15,260 --> 00:18:15,980
First try!

344
00:18:16,660 --> 00:18:18,260
I scored a rainbow diamond!

345
00:18:18,820 --> 00:18:19,960
It's just like I thought.

346
00:18:20,280 --> 00:18:21,420
This little die is the key

347
00:18:21,420 --> 00:18:23,460
to really hitting it big time in this city.

348
00:18:23,860 --> 00:18:25,420
But what if you roll worse luck?

349
00:18:25,600 --> 00:18:27,700
Things could get really scary really quickly.

350
00:18:28,100 --> 00:18:29,140
Don't worry about it.

351
00:18:29,140 --> 00:18:30,820
It's not like it's gonna kill me, right?

352
00:18:31,200 --> 00:18:31,600
Huh?

353
00:18:31,800 --> 00:18:33,020
Oh, no!

354
00:18:33,180 --> 00:18:34,640
A slot machine exploded!

355
00:18:35,420 --> 00:18:37,080
I knew something was wrong.

356
00:18:37,320 --> 00:18:39,840
That guy just hit the jackpot five times in a row.

357
00:18:40,240 --> 00:18:41,780
And he was acting weird.

358
00:18:42,160 --> 00:18:44,200
He kept rolling some funny-looking die.

359
00:18:44,900 --> 00:18:45,420
Whoa!

360
00:18:45,720 --> 00:18:47,320
His face is mushed!

361
00:18:47,580 --> 00:18:47,860
Look!

362
00:18:49,780 --> 00:18:50,240
Okay.

363
00:18:50,500 --> 00:18:52,320
So my vote is that we make the trade.

364
00:18:52,320 --> 00:18:55,280
Yeah, we want all S-ranked cards and above.

365
00:18:55,280 --> 00:18:57,120
And the sooner we obtain them, the better.

366
00:18:57,540 --> 00:18:57,900
True.

367
00:18:58,560 --> 00:19:00,280
But as for A-rank and below...

368
00:19:02,520 --> 00:19:04,840
Roll.

369
00:19:05,220 --> 00:19:06,240
Please spare me!

370
00:19:06,300 --> 00:19:07,300
I'm begging you!

371
00:19:07,660 --> 00:19:08,380
Don't worry.

372
00:19:08,480 --> 00:19:09,880
It's only your third time.

373
00:19:10,040 --> 00:19:11,260
You'll be all right.

374
00:19:11,260 --> 00:19:16,080
But I knew a guy, and he had the worst luck on his first roll, and he died.

375
00:19:16,340 --> 00:19:17,040
Spare me!

376
00:19:17,200 --> 00:19:21,520
If I roll worst luck, that means I'll be hit for every time the other players rolled great luck!

377
00:19:22,760 --> 00:19:24,180
That's not my problem.

378
00:19:24,720 --> 00:19:25,180
Roll it.

379
00:19:25,660 --> 00:19:28,200
Or perhaps you'd rather die now.

380
00:19:28,200 --> 00:19:37,800
Oh, please!

381
00:19:42,600 --> 00:19:43,660
There, see?

382
00:19:44,200 --> 00:19:46,320
It's pretty rare to get worst luck.

383
00:19:46,840 --> 00:19:48,840
Now we'll use the lottery card.

384
00:19:50,380 --> 00:19:53,940
We won number 75, the wild luck Alexandrite.

385
00:19:54,100 --> 00:19:54,700
You got that?

386
00:19:54,700 --> 00:19:58,460
And if you're able to obtain one for us, we'll set you free.

387
00:19:58,700 --> 00:19:59,200
Please.

388
00:19:59,460 --> 00:20:00,120
Oh, please.

389
00:20:00,600 --> 00:20:01,720
Lottery on!

390
00:20:04,140 --> 00:20:04,700
Well?

391
00:20:05,820 --> 00:20:07,000
Number 76.

392
00:20:07,480 --> 00:20:08,940
Ooh, so close.

393
00:20:09,320 --> 00:20:11,180
I guess today's not your lucky day.

394
00:20:11,360 --> 00:20:11,680
Right.

395
00:20:11,880 --> 00:20:12,380
One more.

396
00:20:12,620 --> 00:20:12,920
Roll.

397
00:20:13,200 --> 00:20:13,960
One more time.

398
00:20:14,060 --> 00:20:14,800
One more time.

399
00:20:15,120 --> 00:20:16,800
Time to see what Motorike's got.

400
00:20:16,980 --> 00:20:18,920
It's time to shine just one more time.

401
00:20:21,740 --> 00:20:23,380
So it didn't happen, huh?

402
00:20:23,380 --> 00:20:25,740
Well, what now, Gen?

403
00:20:26,040 --> 00:20:27,900
Should we make the first move or what?

404
00:20:28,540 --> 00:20:31,320
Like I said, combat is our last resort.

405
00:20:31,620 --> 00:20:32,560
It's still early.

406
00:20:32,940 --> 00:20:33,540
Hold on.

407
00:20:33,720 --> 00:20:35,860
We're trying to stay one step ahead of them, right?

408
00:20:36,560 --> 00:20:40,380
But as soon as we commit, further negotiations will be completely impossible.

409
00:20:40,380 --> 00:20:43,180
What do you have in mind?

410
00:20:43,600 --> 00:20:47,860
We use Tax Collector's Gauntlet combined with Risky Dice.

411
00:20:49,760 --> 00:20:50,820
I understand.

412
00:20:51,300 --> 00:20:54,620
You're saying we use that to steal eight cards from them immediately.

413
00:20:55,140 --> 00:20:57,220
But that'd definitely be dangerous.

414
00:20:57,880 --> 00:21:00,940
If someone rolls worst luck, then they'll probably die.

415
00:21:00,940 --> 00:21:04,700
And this job is too important to leave to them.

416
00:21:05,940 --> 00:21:06,820
Come on.

417
00:21:07,160 --> 00:21:08,240
We've come this far.

418
00:21:08,340 --> 00:21:09,240
Let's clear the game.

419
00:21:12,960 --> 00:21:13,780
Hey, Gen.

420
00:21:14,140 --> 00:21:14,960
What are you doing?

421
00:21:15,600 --> 00:21:17,240
I've told you this before.

422
00:21:17,600 --> 00:21:19,760
When we take a big risk like this one,

423
00:21:20,080 --> 00:21:21,440
we share the danger.

424
00:21:21,440 --> 00:21:34,920
It's Tezgera.

425
00:21:35,180 --> 00:21:35,980
What'll it be?

426
00:21:36,460 --> 00:21:37,120
We're in.

427
00:21:37,360 --> 00:21:38,860
You have yourself a deal.

428
00:21:43,860 --> 00:21:45,220
I'm gonna do it.

429
00:21:45,460 --> 00:21:46,820
Just one more time.

430
00:21:47,240 --> 00:21:48,960
I already said I'm gonna do it.

431
00:21:48,960 --> 00:21:51,820
So I'm gonna do it!

432
00:21:54,100 --> 00:21:55,060
All right.

433
00:21:55,280 --> 00:21:56,780
On to the next city.

434
00:21:57,040 --> 00:21:58,000
Let's go!

435
00:22:00,740 --> 00:22:04,680
Gon and the rest of his team have begun working to beat the game.

436
00:22:05,140 --> 00:22:07,640
The story's climax is drawing near.

437
00:22:07,640 --> 00:22:13,860
I'll walk away.

438
00:22:14,000 --> 00:22:28,580
Let's go!

439
00:22:28,580 --> 00:22:58,560
I'll see you next time.

440
00:22:58,580 --> 00:23:21,240
Coming up, the Great Island Tutorial!

441
00:23:28,580 --> 00:23:58,560
I'll see you next time.

